{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"66ee6db4-ba8b-4856-b77f-96c3e619185c","title":"Exponential growth and decay"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"66ee6db4-ba8b-4856-b77f-96c3e619185c","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Exponential change multiplies a quantity by the same factor each equal time interval. We will compare growth and decay starting from one.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Exponential growth and decay"},{"op":"equation","id":"rule","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"y=A\\,b^t\\qquad(A>0,\\ b>0)"},{"op":"axes","id":"axes","region":"right","x":{"min":0,"max":3,"label":"time t"},"y":{"min":0,"max":8,"label":"quantity y"}}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"66ee6db4-ba8b-4856-b77f-96c3e619185c","step":{"id":"s2","script":"With a factor of two, the quantity doubles each interval: one, two, four, eight. Equal time steps produce increasingly large additions.","ops":[{"op":"curve","id":"growth","axes_id":"axes","expr":"2^x","domain":[0,3]},{"op":"equation","id":"growthrule","anchor":{"el":"rule","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"y=2^t\\qquad b=2>1"},{"op":"equation","id":"growthvalues","anchor":{"el":"growthrule","side":"below","gap":0.05},"latex":"1\\ \\to\\ 2\\ \\to\\ 4\\ \\to\\ 8"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"66ee6db4-ba8b-4856-b77f-96c3e619185c","step":{"id":"s3","script":"With a factor of one-half, the quantity halves each interval. It approaches zero but remains positive; it never subtracts a fixed amount.","ops":[{"op":"curve","id":"decay","axes_id":"axes","expr":"(1/2)^x","domain":[0,3]},{"op":"equation","id":"decayrule","anchor":{"el":"growthvalues","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"y=\\left(\\frac12\\right)^t\\qquad 0<b<1"},{"op":"equation","id":"decayvalues","anchor":{"el":"decayrule","side":"below","gap":0.05},"latex":"1\\ \\to\\ \\frac12\\ \\to\\ \\frac14\\ \\to\\ \\frac18"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"If a quantity is multiplied by 0.8 each hour, is it growing or decaying, and by what percentage?","expected_gist":"Decaying by 20 percent each hour, because 80 percent remains."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"66ee6db4-ba8b-4856-b77f-96c3e619185c","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Both curves start at one because any positive base to the zero power equals one. Generally, A sets the start; b sets the multiplier.","ops":[{"op":"point","id":"initial","construct":{"kind":"along","element_id":"growth","t":0},"label":"start: 1"},{"op":"equation","id":"initialrule","anchor":{"el":"decayvalues","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"y(0)=A\\,b^0=A"},{"op":"text","id":"summary","anchor":{"el":"initialrule","side":"below","gap":0.05},"content":"Same multiplier, not same addition."}],"checkpoint":null}}
